WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.625
Lately, I’ve been haunted by a recurring dream. Although I reluctantly call it that. What I experience is far too deliberate.

00:00:05.925 --> 00:00:11.640
»Visitation« seems a more fitting term; they won’t leave me alone. It’s as if they’ve returned, and there’s nowhere I can hide.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:16.845
Back then, I thought that if I shut my eyes for long enough, I would realise that they were just an illusion.

00:00:17.145 --> 00:00:22.005
Given how many times I moved their names between the registers, I convinced myself I was just seeing things.

00:00:22.305 --> 00:00:32.025
But every time I thought they had disappeared for good, I could hear the distinct sound of shuffling footsteps on the other side of the plexiglass partition, their faces materialising before me, if only for a second.

00:00:32.325 --> 00:00:38.625
I’m not sure how they kept coming back. I followed the procedure exactly as I had been instructed during training. I never missed a session.

00:00:38.925 --> 00:00:44.550
I did everything I was supposed to; almost obsessively, I compared the computerized records with the records we kept by hand.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:50.970
I was responsible for taking the minutes of the meetings, which we then forwarded on. I recorded everything down to the smallest detail.

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:56.040
I even learnt certain passages by heart so that I could carry out the proceedings with absolute precision.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:01:03.225
I can still almost recite them all; they are constantly swirling around in my head. Each time I wake up, it feels as though a hand is squeezing my heart.

00:01:03.525 --> 00:01:07.530
Its fingertips have extended into sharp claws that are slowly tearing through the tissue.

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:13.590
I forget how to breathe, to the point where I nearly faint and sweat drips down my forehead. Then I realise that I have shouted.

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:17.890
You might call this anxiety, but I know the hand is real. I recognise it. It’s mine.
